1
00:00:00,807 --> 00:00:02,207
(Howard:)that ladies pretend
they don't do

2
00:00:02,209 --> 00:00:04,879
(Howard:)even though they do?

3
00:00:06,879 --> 00:00:08,949
(Sheldon:)You know...

4
00:00:08,949 --> 00:00:11,579
which yogurt I mean.

5
00:00:11,585 --> 00:00:14,415
(Howard:)I didn't touch it.
Must have been Stuart.

6
00:00:14,421 --> 00:00:16,291
(sighs)
Maybe Raj is right.

7
00:00:16,289 --> 00:00:18,689
(Bernadette:)Maybe it's time we tell him
he needs to move out.

8
00:00:18,692 --> 00:00:20,562
(Howard:)We should have done
it months ago.

9
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,160
(Bernadette:)I know, but his store
was reopening,

10
00:00:22,162 --> 00:00:24,692
(Bernadette:)and then there were the
holidays, and then he was sick.

11
00:00:24,698 --> 00:00:26,128
(groans)
Yeah, right.

12
00:00:26,132 --> 00:00:28,332
(Howard:)Sick. He didn't have jaundice.

13
00:00:28,335 --> 00:00:30,605
(Howard:)He just looks like that.

14
00:00:35,741 --> 00:00:38,411
(Emily:)All right.
Tonight's the night.

15
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:39,611
(Howard:)Agreed.

16
00:00:39,613 --> 00:00:42,113
(Howard:)When he gets home, I'm
dropping the hammer.

17
00:00:42,115 --> 00:00:44,115
(Bernadette:)Ooh, I like
when you take charge.

18
00:00:44,117 --> 00:00:46,347
(Howard:)Oh, I'm not taking charge--
you're the hammer.

19
00:00:53,192 --> 00:00:55,192
(Stuart:)So...

20
00:00:55,195 --> 00:00:57,495
(Leonard:)why haven't we
picked a date?

21
00:00:57,497 --> 00:00:58,527
(Penny:)You know why.

22
00:00:58,532 --> 00:01:00,022
(Leonard:)Well, of course I know why.

